WEBVTT

NOTE Captions for "Losing a device, and getting back in" (Identity). No audio
NOTE track yet; these captions carry the narration. Source: learn/manim/scripts/recovery.md

00:00.000 --> 00:25.000
Two keys, two jobs. Your PIN unlocks one device, and it is local to that device; we never see it. Your Secret Key recovers your whole account. It is shown to you exactly once, and you write it down and keep it safe, like the deed to a house.

00:25.000 --> 00:55.000
Here is how recovery works. The server keeps a copy of your account key, but it keeps it locked in a box. Only your Secret Key opens that box, and the server does not have your Secret Key. So the company cannot open your account, and neither can anyone who steals the box.

00:55.000 --> 01:25.000
To sign in on a new device you have two ways. The easy way is to approve it from a device you already have: the two show the same six-digit code, you confirm they match, and they agree on a private key in plain sight of the server. The other way is your Secret Key, the same recovery without a second device. Either way, the new device then joins every group you are in, from today forward, with no old history, which is the boundary from Topic 4.

01:25.000 --> 01:50.000
And one hard rule. If you lose your Secret Key and every device you were ever signed in on, the account starts fresh. No one holds a spare key to your account, including us. That is the price of a door only you can open, and it is the point.
